{"status":"completed","summary":"Established a persistent AIDE integrity baseline for /etc on node1. The 1,452-entry baseline uses SHA-512 plus permissions, ownership, size, ACL, SELinux, and xattr checks. Daily reporting is enabled, change detection was proven, and persistence was verified across a node restart.","actions_performed":["Installed AIDE 0.19.2.","Created /etc/aide-etc.conf scoped to /etc.","Created and enabled the persistent daily aide-etc-check.timer; reports go to the system journal and /var/log/aide/etc.log.","Initialized the protected baseline at /var/lib/aide/etc.db.gz with root-only permissions.","Proved a modified file is reported with its size and SHA-512 changes, then restored it and confirmed a clean check.","Restarted node1 safely and verified its boot identity changed.","Confirmed the timer, configuration, database, and clean integrity state recovered after restart."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Persistent /etc integrity baseline","command_ids":["cmd-1778d1c5bfc743a8","cmd-3c29bf6a4e3542b1"],"summary":"AIDE configuration covers /etc, the database contains 1,452 entries, the daily timer is enabled and active, and the final check is clean."},{"requirement":"Later file changes can be identified and reported","command_ids":["cmd-fba5b73747394e12"],"summary":"A controlled modification to /etc/aide-etc.conf was reported as one changed file with differing size and SHA-512 hash; restoration returned the baseline to clean."},{"requirement":"node1 mandatory restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-c4a097eb50f34ddd","cmd-ffc814dcd0a94e88","cmd-c6310cabfb744fd9","cmd-3c29bf6a4e3542b1"],"summary":"Captured healthy pre-restart state and boot ID 254597f8-4ac9-4062-8be8-44eba1f6d2e9, received native reboot acknowledgement, observed new boot ID 7d8174d3-7d1a-4766-ab5e-a28420ad74b3, and verified the active timer, persisted baseline, and clean post-restart state."}]}
